.TH ssh 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
ssh \- the simple shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ssh
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read this before typing it.
.B ssh
here is the
.I simple shell
from UZI: a small command interpreter, and nothing whatever to do with
the secure shell.  It makes no network connection and takes no host
name.
.PP
It reads commands, finds them on
.BR PATH ,
runs them, and understands redirection and background jobs.  It exists
because it is small; the shell you actually get at login is
.BR sh (1),
the V7 Bourne shell, which is a great deal more capable.
.SH BUILT-IN COMMANDS
.B cd
.BR exit ,
.BR pwd ,
.BR sync ,
.BR umask ,
.BR kill ,
.B fg
and
.BR bg .
An argument of the form
.I name=value
sets an environment variable.
.SH REDIRECTION
.BR < ,
.B >
and
.B &
work as you would expect.  Up to 16 arguments to a command.
.SH NOTES
There is no scripting here: no
.BR if ,
no
.BR while ,
no functions, no shell variables beyond the environment.  Write scripts
for
.BR sh (1).
.PP
To reach another machine over the network there is no client on this
system.  Go the other way:
.BR httpd (1)
serves from the board, and
.BR htget (1)
and
.BR tlsget (1)
fetch from it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR htget (1),
.BR httpd (1)
